                <pb facs="0170" n="88" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg88"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Sanford to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 277.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 29,1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Mourning has been brought to many families
                    here by the news from Mexico of the destruction of a detachment of the Belgian
                    legion in a combat at Tamcaburo, in the State of Michoacan, on the 11th of
                    April. It is stated in the published reports that the whole detachment of about
                    300 men were either killed, wounded, or taken prisoners. Among the killed is a
                    son of the minister of war, General de Chazal, who was a captain, and seven
                    other officers.* *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. S. SANFORD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
